## Deliberately not shipped

**Chicago and Monaco font files.** The design references Chicago (as the
ChicagoFLF revival) and Monaco. Neither binary is in this repository or in its
history. The `@font-face` rules resolve them with `local()` only, so a machine
that already has them uses them and every other machine falls back to Public
Sans and IBM Plex Mono, which the project's own style sheet names as the
stand-ins.

**Macintosh icon set.** The design language descends from Susan Kare's 1984
Macintosh icons. Those icons are Apple's. None of them are in this repository
or in its history. The eight icons the system calls for are pending an original
redraw in the same 1-bit grammar; until that lands, no icons ship.

The rule this repository follows: assets whose provenance is not clean never
enter the history, because git history is permanent and deleting a file later
does not remove it.
